1. INTRODUCTION
The Campus Food Delivery and Order Management System is a console-based Python application designed to help a campus food delivery service manage customers, food items, orders, order totals, delivery information and order status. It replaces manual record keeping with a simple computerized solution.
The program uses functions, lists and dictionaries to organize information and saves records in a JSON file so that data remains available after the program is closed.
2. PROBLEM STATEMENT
Campus food businesses may receive many orders from students and staff. Manual management can cause incorrect totals, missing customer information, duplicate records and difficulty tracking deliveries. This system provides a simple computerized way to manage these activities accurately.
3. AIM
To design and implement a Python-based Campus Food Delivery and Order Management System that records customers and food orders, calculates costs, tracks order status and preserves records between program runs.
4. OBJECTIVES
Register and store customer information.
Maintain a menu of food items and prices.
Create orders containing one or more food items.
Calculate order totals accurately.
Record delivery location and contact information.
Update and display order status.
Search for orders by ID or customer name.
Display basic order and sales statistics.
Validate user input and handle common errors.
Save and reload records using JSON.
