6. SYSTEM DESIGN
The system is divided into small functions. This makes the program easier to understand, test and maintain.
Menu management: stores food names, categories and prices.
Customer management: stores names, phone numbers and delivery locations.
Order management: creates orders containing multiple items.
Payment calculation: calculates subtotal, delivery fee and total.
Status management: tracks Pending, Preparing, Out for Delivery, Delivered and Cancelled.
Search: finds orders using order ID or customer name.
Reports: displays orders and basic statistics.
Persistence: stores records in campus_food_data.json.
7. DATA STRUCTURES
The project uses dictionaries and lists. A dictionary stores related values using meaningful keys, while lists store multiple records. Customers are stored in a dictionary using phone numbers as keys, and orders are stored in a list of dictionaries.
